	(text "USB 2.0 interface (FT2232H)" (at 234.95 63.5 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left))
		(uuid "fb833940-8488-45d0-99c4-caebc021688b"))
	(text "DUAL-CHANNEL 12-BIT 10 MS/s USB ADC  (see DESIGN.md for options and rationale)\nSignal path (per channel): BNC -> 1 Mohm || ~19 pF input, compensated /10.06 divider (2 x 453k + 100k)\n  -> BAV99 clamp to +/-3.3 V -> OPA810 FET-input unity buffer -> THS4521 FDA (G = 1, VOCM = ADC VCM 1.5 V)\n  -> 49.9R/33pF RC -> LTC2290 dual 12-bit ADC (2 Vpp diff span, SENSE = VDD).\n  +/-10 V at BNC = +/-0.994 V differential at ADC (full scale +/-10.06 V). Trim C104/C204 for flat step response.\nClock: 10.000 MHz Abracon ASE oscillator on the clean +3.0 V rail, star-fed (33R each) to CLKA, CLKB and FPGA GBIN5.\nCapture: iCE40HX4K writes both channels (16 bit/sample, 40 MB/s) to a 32 MB MT48LC16M16A2 SDRAM.\n  0.1 s x 2 ch x 10 MS/s x 2 B = 4 MB required; 32 MB holds 0.8 s.\nHost link: FT2232H, USB 2.0 High Speed. Ch A = 245 synchronous FIFO (60 MHz, ~35-40 MB/s) to the FPGA.\n  Ch B = MPSSE: programs the W25Q32 config flash and drives CRESET/reads CDONE (iceprog -I B).\n  93LC56 EEPROM sets ch A to 245 FIFO mode; host enables sync FIFO with SetBitMode(0x40).\nPower: USB-C receptacle wired as USB 2.0 device (5.1k Rd on CC1/CC2), 500 mA default USB budget.\n  Estimated draw ~300 mA at 5 V (see DESIGN.md), so USB 2.0 power is sufficient.\n  TPS62162 buck 3.3 V digital; AP2112 1.2 V core; LP5907 3.3 V and 3.0 V analog LDOs; LM27761 -3.3 V.\nUnverified items to check against datasheets before fab: LM27761 FB reference, LTC2290 REF bypass network,\n  iCE40 GNDPLL handling, FT2232H ch B MPSSE use while ch A is in 245 FIFO mode, crystal load caps." (at 30.48 95.25 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "9b9b8ccc-c767-4afb-b841-fbf1750ba8c5"))

